  "evidence": "The timer manifest registers the custom descriptor; its state allocation is freed and cleared in destroy. The main preset builder registers one callback per preset. The custom builder registers one handler with event filters 11 and 12 on each of three rollers; the callback checks selected values before enabling start.",
  "scope": "Recorded shared UI and event calls, not the timer scheduling backend or every timer state transition. Existing focus-related registration points cover different call sites.",
  "limitations": "The preset event data is a pointer, not a duration integer; changing it incorrectly can crash. Altering events can leave start availability or timer state inconsistent. State slots are not thread barriers; device behavior and recovery remain unverified.",
